   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Corpus Christi College range on Trumpington Street south of the Taylor Library (former bank): dark grey-brown brick Tudor-Gothic, three storeys with stepped gables and battlemented parapet, stone dressings; four wide bays with two-storey canted bay/oriel windows alternating with narrow bays holding pointed-arched doorways or two-light windows; Gothic doorway at the junction with the bank. Bay rhythm counted from Mapillary 347396670530528 and two geograph views; positions spaced evenly."
